{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat README.md && cat notes.json'","aggregated_output":"# notes-mcp\n\nA small remote MCP server for my garden notes, meant for Claude Code, Codex\nand Gemini clients. Streamable HTTP, JSON responses, Python standard library.\n\n```\npython3 server.py              # http://127.0.0.1:55632/mcp\nPORT=9000 python3 server.py\n```\n\nTools: `search_notes` (read), `get_note` (read), `add_note` (write, needs\n`Authorization: Bearer dev-token-123` in development).\n\nNot yet listed in any registry. No CI. Logs go to stderr, one JSON line per\ncall.\n[\n  {\"id\": \"n-1\", \"title\": \"Soil pH kit review\", \"body\": \"The cheap colour kit reads 0.5 high against the lab. Fine for trend, not for liming decisions.\", \"tags\": [\"soil\"]},\n  {\"id\": \"n-2\", \"title\": \"Compost thermometer week 3\", \"body\": \"Core at 61C on day 18, turned the pile, back to 55C by day 21. Moisture felt right.\", \"tags\": [\"compost\"]},\n  {\"id\": \"n-3\", \"title\": \"Drip line pressure\", \"body\": \"Emitters past the 30 m mark starve at 1 bar. A second feed from the far end fixed it.\", \"tags\": [\"irrigation\"]},\n  {\"id\": \"n-4\", \"title\": \"First frost dates\", \"body\": \"Ten years of first frost: median Oct 24, earliest Oct 9. Cover beds by Oct 15.\", \"tags\": [\"weather\"]},\n  {\"id\": \"n-5\", \"title\": \"Rain barrel overflow\", \"body\": \"Overflow into the swale, not the path. Added a 50 mm elbow and a leaf screen.\", \"tags\": [\"water\"]}\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
